course: dictionary
lesson: 11130
title: Why and the reason it matters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Why» is a question word. It asks for the reason or cause of something. «Why is the sky blue?» asks for a cause, so a good answer tells you because of something.
explain: «Why» can also join a reason to what happens: «That is why I am late.» Here why links the reason to the result. Check it by swapping in because: «That is because I am late» still makes sense, so why means the reason here.
explain: «Why» can show surprise, as in «Why, it's you!» Context tells you which job the word is doing: is it asking a question, joining a reason, or showing surprise?
fact: Why is a question word. It asks for a reason.
fact: «Why» can join a reason to a sentence: «That is why I am late.»
fact: «The reason why» is a phrase: the reason why something happens is its cause.
fact: «Why not?» is a casual way to say yes, let's do it.
fact: In science, why questions ask for causes, like why ice floats. In maths, «Explain why» means show your reasoning, not just the answer.
exercise: «If something goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» What does why ask for here? | *The reason something happened | A way to say hello | The name of a plane | A colour
exercise: «Your dose depends on your age and weight, which is why yours differs from your little sister's.» Here why joins what to what? | A question to a number | Two colours | A name to a place | *Your age and weight to your dose being different
exercise: Ella's friend asks, «Do you want to go to the park? Why not?» What does «Why not?» mean here? | *Yes, let's go | Why did we go | No, we must never go | Go away now
test: «Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it.» In this sentence, why means | A kind of food | A loud shout of surprise | The name of a place | *The reason something is dangerous
test: Which sentence uses why to ask for a reason? | That is why I am late | Why not? | *Why is the sky blue? | Why, it's you!
exam: «Explain why the ice floats.» What is this task asking you to do? | *Give the reason the ice floats | Name a colour | Draw a picture of ice | Count the ice cubes
